@* Marks a change that has NOT happened yet, so a conditional entry is never
   read as a decision already taken. The wording is deliberately "may" and
   "depends on" rather than anything that sounds settled — a foreseeable change
   is conditional precisely because its condition is unresolved, and copy that
   drifts into sounding like a commitment turns a warning into a promise the
   service cannot keep. *@

<span class="foreseeable-badge">
    <span class="foreseeable-badge__mark" aria-hidden="true">•</span>
    @Label
</span>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string Label { get; set; } = "Not decided yet — depends on a match still to be played";
}
